      "text": "To find the matrix \\(\\mathbf{P}\\) for projecting onto the vector \\(\\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we need to compute the projection matrix \\(\\mathbf{P}\\). The projection matrix \\(\\mathbf{P}\\) that projects any vector \\(\\mathbf{v}\\) onto a vector \\(\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}\\) is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{P} = \\frac{\\mathbf{a} \\mathbf{a}^T}{\\mathbf{a}^T \\mathbf{a}}\n\\]\n\nFirst, we calculate \\(\\mathbf{a} \\mathbf{a}^T\\):\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\mathbf{a}^T = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 & -2 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 9 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 4 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(\\mathbf{a}^T \\mathbf{a}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a}^T \\mathbf{a} = (-3)^2 + (-2)^2 = 9 + 4 = 13\n\\]\n\nThus, the projection matrix \\(\\mathbf{P}\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{P} = \\frac{1}{13} \\begin{pmatrix} 9 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 4 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{9}{13} & \\frac{6}{13} \\\\ \\frac{6}{13} & \\frac{4}{13} \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nTo find the inverse of \\(\\mathbf{P}\\), we need to check if \\(\\mathbf{P}\\) is invertible. A matrix is invertible if and only if its determinant is non-zero. The determinant of \\(\\mathbf{P}\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\det(\\mathbf{P}) = \\left( \\frac{9}{13} \\right) \\left( \\frac{4}{13} \\right) - \\left( \\frac{6}{13} \\right) \\left( \\frac{6}{13} \\right) = \\frac{36}{169} - \\frac{36}{169} = 0\n\\]\n\nSince the determinant is zero, the matrix \\(\\mathbf{P}\\) is not invertible. Therefore, the inverse of \\(\\mathbf{P}\\) does not exist. The answer is the zero matrix.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\end{pmatrix}}\n\\]",
